{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba packages/contracts/node_modules/@chainlink/contracts/src/v0.8/vrf/dev/VRFV2PlusWrapperConsumerBase.sol | tail -65; nl -ba packages/contracts/src/RaffleFactory.sol | sed -n '58,93p'\"","aggregated_output":"    54\t   * @param _requestConfirmations is the number of confirmations to wait before fulfilling the\n    55\t   *        request. A higher number of confirmations increases security by reducing the likelihood\n    56\t   *        that a chain re-org changes a published randomness outcome.\n    57\t   * @param _numWords is the number of random words to request.\n    58\t   *\n    59\t   * @return requestId is the VRF V2+ request ID of the newly created randomness request.\n    60\t   */\n    61\t  // solhint-disable-next-line chainlink-solidity/prefix-internal-functions-with-underscore\n    62\t  function requestRandomness(\n    63\t    uint32 _callbackGasLimit,\n    64\t    uint16 _requestConfirmations,\n    65\t    uint32 _numWords,\n    66\t    bytes memory extraArgs\n    67\t  ) internal returns (uint256 requestId, uint256 reqPrice) {\n    68\t    reqPrice = i_vrfV2PlusWrapper.calculateRequestPrice(_callbackGasLimit, _numWords);\n    69\t    i_linkToken.transferAndCall(\n    70\t      address(i_vrfV2PlusWrapper), reqPrice, abi.encode(_callbackGasLimit, _requestConfirmations, _numWords, extraArgs)\n    71\t    );\n    72\t    return (i_vrfV2PlusWrapper.lastRequestId(), reqPrice);\n    73\t  }\n    74\t\n    75\t  // solhint-disable-next-line chainlink-solidity/prefix-internal-functions-with-underscore\n    76\t  function requestRandomnessPayInNative(\n    77\t    uint32 _callbackGasLimit,\n    78\t    uint16 _requestConfirmations,\n    79\t    uint32 _numWords,\n    80\t    bytes memory extraArgs\n    81\t  ) internal returns (uint256 requestId, uint256 requestPrice) {\n    82\t    requestPrice = i_vrfV2PlusWrapper.calculateRequestPriceNative(_callbackGasLimit, _numWords);\n    83\t    return (\n    84\t      i_vrfV2PlusWrapper.requestRandomWordsInNative{value: requestPrice}(\n    85\t        _callbackGasLimit, _requestConfirmations, _numWords, extraArgs\n    86\t      ),\n    87\t      requestPrice\n    88\t    );\n    89\t  }\n    90\t\n    91\t  /**\n    92\t   * @notice fulfillRandomWords handles the VRF V2 wrapper response. The consuming contract must\n    93\t   * @notice implement it.\n    94\t   *\n    95\t   * @param _requestId is the VRF V2 request ID.\n    96\t   * @param _randomWords is the randomness result.\n    97\t   */\n    98\t  // solhint-disable-next-line chainlink-solidity/prefix-internal-functions-with-underscore\n    99\t  function fulfillRandomWords(uint256 _requestId, uint256[] memory _randomWords) internal virtual;\n   100\t\n   101\t  function rawFulfillRandomWords(uint256 _requestId, uint256[] memory _randomWords) external {\n   102\t    address vrfWrapperAddr = address(i_vrfV2PlusWrapper);\n   103\t    if (msg.sender != vrfWrapperAddr) {\n   104\t      revert OnlyVRFWrapperCanFulfill(msg.sender, vrfWrapperAddr);\n   105\t    }\n   106\t    fulfillRandomWords(_requestId, _randomWords);\n   107\t  }\n   108\t\n   109\t  /// @notice getBalance returns the native balance of the consumer contract\n   110\t  function getBalance() public view returns (uint256) {\n   111\t    return address(this).balance;\n   112\t  }\n   113\t\n   114\t  /// @notice getLinkToken returns the link token contract\n   115\t  function getLinkToken() public view returns (LinkTokenInterface) {\n   116\t    return i_linkToken;\n   117\t  }\n   118\t}\n    58\t    /// @notice Deploys the ownerless factory and its locked raffle implementation with one immutable configuration.\n    59\t    /// @dev The quote token must report exactly six decimals; the wrapper and quote token must contain deployed code.\n    60\t    ///      Deployment tooling must supply and verify the target chain's official USDC address because the constructor\n    61\t    ///      cannot prove token identity from metadata.\n    62\t    /// @param quoteToken_ Target chain's official six-decimal USDC contract trusted by every raffle.\n    63\t    /// @param vrfWrapper_ Official Chainlink VRF v2.5 native direct-funding wrapper for the target chain.\n    64\t    /// @param protocolTreasury_ Immutable protocol-fee recipient used by every raffle.\n    65\t    constructor(address quoteToken_, address vrfWrapper_, address protocolTreasury_) {\n    66\t        _requireContract(quoteToken_);\n    67\t        _requireContract(vrfWrapper_);\n    68\t        if (protocolTreasury_ == address(0)) revert ZeroAddress();\n    69\t\n    70\t        uint8 quoteDecimals = 0;\n    71\t        try IERC20Metadata(quoteToken_).decimals() returns (uint8 decimals_) {\n    72\t            quoteDecimals = decimals_;\n    73\t        } catch {\n    74\t            revert UnsupportedQuoteToken(quoteToken_);\n    75\t        }\n    76\t        if (quoteDecimals != RaffleConstants.QUOTE_TOKEN_DECIMALS) {\n    77\t            revert InvalidQuoteTokenDecimals(quoteDecimals, RaffleConstants.QUOTE_TOKEN_DECIMALS);\n    78\t        }\n    79\t\n    80\t        if (protocolTreasury_ == address(this) || protocolTreasury_ == quoteToken_ || protocolTreasury_ == vrfWrapper_)\n    81\t        {\n    82\t            revert UnsafeProtocolDestination(protocolTreasury_);\n    83\t        }\n    84\t\n    85\t        quoteToken = quoteToken_;\n    86\t        vrfWrapper = vrfWrapper_;\n    87\t        protocolTreasury = protocolTreasury_;\n    88\t\n    89\t        address implementation = address(new Raffle(quoteToken_, vrfWrapper_));\n    90\t        if (protocolTreasury_ == implementation) revert UnsafeProtocolDestination(protocolTreasury_);\n    91\t        raffleImplementation = implementation;\n    92\t    }\n    93\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"_kritt_extractor_helper\":true,\"stub\":true,\"stub_explanation\":\"No supported vulnerability in the reviewed flow. Raffle.buyEntries is external and nonpayable; Solidity rejects insufficient calldata, invalid address/uint128 encodings, and nonzero msg.value before the modifier or purchase body executes. Factory-created ERC-1167 clones preserve these checks and propagate reverts, preventing USDC transfers or raffle/ticket state changes on rejected calls.\",\"results\":[]}"}}
